    <!--
        `26-91`: the English translation of `values/strings.xml` — nothing reads this file yet
        (`26-92` wires `AppCompatDelegate.setApplicationLocales`); it exists so that item has
        somewhere correct to point to. Every key here has a matching key in `values/strings.xml`,
        and every value is a natural English sentence, not a literal rendering.

        Terminology carried over from `ago-console`'s own `en.ts`/`ru.ts` (the same facts, worded the
        same way on both surfaces, the same rule this app's own Russian strings already follow for
        `ago-console` parity):
          - «магазин» → "shop" (`ago-console/src/i18n/en.ts`'s own `installKeyPanelDescription`:
            "This key tells the chat widget which shop it belongs to"), never "site" — "site" is
            reserved for `tenancySwitcherLabel`'s own formal "Site" (not used in this app's own
            Russian strings, which all say «магазин»).
          - «Мастер» → "Master", not "Worker" — `ago-console`'s own `navCalendarWorkers` is "Masters"
            and `calendarBookingsDescription` reads "Confirmed bookings, by day and by master"; "Worker"
            is that console's own back-office/setup term (`calendarWorkerFieldLabel`), a different
            screen's register than this app's operator-facing booking card.
          - «Оператор»/«Посетитель» → "Operator"/"Visitor", `docs/vision.md`'s own actor names.

        Two flagged judgement calls with no settled precedent found in `ago-console` or `docs/vision.md`,
        left here rather than guessed silently (both are placeholder rows behind
        `PlaceholderDestinationScreen` today, so getting either wrong costs nothing to fix):
          - `more_administration_billing_row` ("Тариф и оплата") → "Plan & billing" — `ago-console`
            only has a bare "Billing" (`billingTitle`), with no equivalent that also names "тариф"
            (tier/plan); this adds "Plan" to keep both halves of the Russian compound.
          - `team_chat_admin_badge` ("Владелец") → "Owner" — literal, no console equivalent for this
            specific badge (`operatorsTeamRoleAdmin` is "Administrator", a different role than "Владелец"
            here).

        Plural forms (`conversation_row_elapsed_*_one/_few/_many`, `conversation_row_unread_*`):
        `ElapsedText.kt`'s own `russianPluralStringResource` hand-picks one of the three resource ids
        by Russian's mod-10/mod-100 grammar (CLDR "ru": one/few/many), not through Android's own
        `<plurals>` — deliberately, per that function's doc comment, because `<plurals>` would pick its
        bucket from the *device's* locale rather than the resource file actually in play. English only
        has a one/other rule, so `_few` and `_many` hold the identical English plural text below (there
        is no third form to distinguish). This does **not** make the pair correct once a locale switch
        exists: the selection function's own Russian "one" bucket also fires for 21, 31, 101… (any count
        ending in 1 except 11), and English wants the plural there ("21 minutes", not "21 minute").
        Nothing reads this file today (`26-91`'s own scope excludes any language switch), so this is
        latent, not live - but `26-92` or a follow-up must adapt the selection itself (a real
        `<plurals>` per locale, or a locale-aware wrapper) before ever pointing it at these strings;
        translating the text alone cannot fix a selection-function bug. Flagged for the author rather
        than silently patched, since fixing the algorithm is out of this item's own declared scope.
    -->
